~ citizen_farmer

Farmer: These are difficult times in Mexico.

Farmer: For many years, President Porfirio Díaz ruled the country.

Farmer: At first he brought stability, but over time many people felt his rule had become a dictatorship.

Farmer: Many farmers lost their land and had little voice in the government.

- Why were people unhappy?
    Farmer: Because Díaz stayed in power for decades and elections were not truly fair.
    => END

- What is a dictatorship?
    Farmer: A dictatorship is when one leader holds most of the power and people have little say in government.
    => END

